{"5380130":{"success":true,"data":{"type":"game","name":"Stillwater: Coastal Maine","steam_appid":5380130,"required_age":0,"is_free":false,"detailed_description":"<strong>Come in. Stay a while.<\/strong><br><br>An old captain's house above the Atlantic. A library lined with books. Beyond the garden, a path through the pines and granite ledges at the water's edge.<br><br><strong>Stillwater: Coastal Maine<\/strong> is a small, first-person retreat on an imagined stretch of the Maine coast. Explore the house and shore, choose the light and weather, and spend a little time in a place that feels familiar.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Find your favorite corner<\/h2>Walk from the painted kitchen to the book-lined library, look out from the room above the roof, or settle into a chair on the porch. Open a book, switch on a reading lamp, and listen to the coast. Save a favorite view to return to on your next visit.<br><br>The library holds 263 classics, complete and unabridged: Austen and Dickens, Jewett and Thoreau, sea stories, poetry and natural history. Take one down and read it by the window.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Small ways to spend an afternoon<\/h2>Cast a line from the old dock and release your catch. Walk the tide line and look for sea glass and shells; a storm washes more ashore, and your finds collect in a jar on the kitchen windowsill. Go for a swim, split some kindling, or play a few notes in the parlor. Upstairs, make a simple color study of the coast and keep it on the easel. Each activity is a quiet way to spend a few minutes during your visit.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Come back in another light<\/h2>A summer porch. Sea fog over the cove. Autumn among the pines. Snow on the grounds and a warm room inside. Choose the season, weather, and time of day, or watch a nor'easter come in over the Atlantic. The same places invite another look as the coast changes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A place close at hand<\/h2>Stillwater is one house, its gardens, and the nearby shore. Its open-ended visits and simple activities are made for a short break or a longer stay. Sea and wind sounds, an optional score of fifteen original pieces for piano and strings, and adjustable walking and viewing controls let you make the visit comfortable.<br><br>If there's interest in Stillwater, we plan to continue creating interesting new locales to visit.","about_the_game":"<strong>Come in. Stay a while.<\/strong><br><br>An old captain's house above the Atlantic. A library lined with books. Beyond the garden, a path through the pines and granite ledges at the water's edge.<br><br><strong>Stillwater: Coastal Maine<\/strong> is a small, first-person retreat on an imagined stretch of the Maine coast. Explore the house and shore, choose the light and weather, and spend a little time in a place that feels familiar.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Find your favorite corner<\/h2>Walk from the painted kitchen to the book-lined library, look out from the room above the roof, or settle into a chair on the porch. Open a book, switch on a reading lamp, and listen to the coast. Save a favorite view to return to on your next visit.<br><br>The library holds 263 classics, complete and unabridged: Austen and Dickens, Jewett and Thoreau, sea stories, poetry and natural history. Take one down and read it by the window.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Small ways to spend an afternoon<\/h2>Cast a line from the old dock and release your catch. Walk the tide line and look for sea glass and shells; a storm washes more ashore, and your finds collect in a jar on the kitchen windowsill. Go for a swim, split some kindling, or play a few notes in the parlor. Upstairs, make a simple color study of the coast and keep it on the easel. Each activity is a quiet way to spend a few minutes during your visit.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Come back in another light<\/h2>A summer porch. Sea fog over the cove. Autumn among the pines. Snow on the grounds and a warm room inside. Choose the season, weather, and time of day, or watch a nor'easter come in over the Atlantic. The same places invite another look as the coast changes.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >A place close at hand<\/h2>Stillwater is one house, its gardens, and the nearby shore. Its open-ended visits and simple activities are made for a short break or a longer stay. Sea and wind sounds, an optional score of fifteen original pieces for piano and strings, and adjustable walking and viewing controls let you make the visit comfortable.<br><br>If there's interest in Stillwater, we plan to continue creating interesting new locales to visit.","short_description":"Make yourself at home on the Maine coast. Explore an old captain's house, read by the window, fish from the dock, and look for sea glass along the tide line. Choose the season, weather, and time of day, or watch a storm come in off the Atlantic. A quiet place to return to at your own pace.","supported_languages":"English","header_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5380130\/6a2db557ae693105047a6d719e1d97a7d6dc1015\/header.jpg?t=1793642457","capsule_image":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5380130\/467fe12441bcd80110aae96489329a8b98f1ba92\/capsule_231x87.jpg?t=1793642457","capsule_imagev5":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5380130\/467fe12441bcd80110aae96489329a8b98f1ba92\/capsule_184x69.jpg?t=1793642457","website":null,"pc_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<br><\/li><li><strong>OS:<\/strong> Windows 11 64-bit<br><\/li><li><strong>Processor:<\/strong> AMD Ryzen 7 8745HS or similar<br><\/li><li><strong>Memory:<\/strong> 8 GB RAM<br><\/li><li><strong>Graphics:<\/strong> AMD Radeon 780M or better<br><\/li><li><strong>Storage:<\/strong> 1 GB available space<br><\/li><li><strong>Additional Notes:<\/strong> SSD recommended. Mouse and keyboard required. Initial visits may take time to prepare the coast.<\/li><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>Requires a 64-bit processor and operating system<\/li><\/ul>"},"mac_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"linux_requirements":{"minimum":"<strong>Minimum:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>","recommended":"<strong>Recommended:<\/strong><br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><\/ul>"},"developers":["Grainwork Studios"],"publishers":["Grainwork Studios"],"price_overview":{"currency":"USD","initial":799,"final":679,"discount_percent":15,"initial_formatted":"$7.99","final_formatted":"$6.79"},"packages":[1858077],"package_groups":[{"name":"default","title":"Buy Stillwater: Coastal Maine","description":"","selection_text":"Select a purchase option","save_text":"","display_type":0,"is_recurring_subscription":"false","subs":[{"packageid":1858077,"percent_savings_text":"-15% ","percent_savings":0,"option_text":"Stillwater: Coastal Maine - <span class=\"discount_original_price\">$7.99<\/span> $6.79","option_description":"","can_get_free_license":"0","is_free_license":false,"price_in_cents_with_discount":679}]}],"platforms":{"windows":true,"mac":false,"linux":false},"categories":[{"id":2,"description":"Single-player"},{"id":62,"description":"Family Sharing"}],"genres":[{"id":"4","description":"Casual"},{"id":"23","description":"Indie"}],"screenshots":[{"id":0,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5380130\/54f5eefdd01d4226b29a0654edb1a4758f4123f5\/ss_54f5eefdd01d4226b29a0654edb1a4758f4123f5.600x338.jpg?t=1793642457","path_full":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/apps\/5380130\/54f5eefdd01d4226b29a0654edb1a4758f4123f5\/ss_54f5eefdd01d4226b29a0654edb1a4758f4123f5.1920x1080.jpg?t=1793642457"},{"id":1,"path_thumbnail":"https:\/\/shared.akamai.steamstatic.com\/store_item_assets\/steam\/ap